  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>AntibesDogz is a family boarding service for dogs based in the Rabiac neighbourhood, north of Antibes. The idea: your dog is hosted by the family running the boarding service, alongside other dogs, with access to a fully fenced garden and an air-conditioned house. The address (825 chemin de Rabiac Estagnol, Villa les Chênes) comes from the legal notices on the antibesdogz.fr website, making it a direct source even though it remains a single one.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>A typical day includes walks, play time and relaxation, with photos sent regularly to owners according to reviews published online. The price advertised on the dedicated page of the website is about €32 per day, and a round-trip transport service between Antibes and the surrounding area is offered from €29. As this is boarding at a private individual's home (rather than a professional facility with kennels), <strong>a prior meeting is recommended</strong> before leaving your dog for several days, and it's best to reconfirm current prices directly with the boarding service when booking.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: as with any boarding at a private individual's home, ask to see the garden and living space before booking, and check for liability insurance covering pet care.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Rabiac neighbourhood lies north of Antibes, between the town and Biot, not far from the Brague river and a few minutes from the Provençal market in old Antibes or Cap d'Antibes.</p>
